
======================================================================================================
DOES THE TWO-LOOP a0 PROTECTION SURVIVE alpha=2? -- and a chronology audit of the corpus
======================================================================================================
  a0 = c H_Lambda/Z, Z = 5.78881 -> 9.3600e-11 m/s^2 canonical; alt 1.1300e-10.
  kappa = 1/2 is Carl's and stays FITTED, not derived.

======================================================================================================
S1. (A) THE ADDITIVE CHANNEL -- closed to ALL ORDERS by a symmetry, and it is KERNEL-FREE
======================================================================================================
  Lane C: 'CLOSED TO ALL ORDERS by the EXACT shift symmetry T -> T + const ... u_mu is a
  homogeneous-degree-0 functional of dT (partial_c u_mu = 0 identically, full nonlinear sqrt),
  so Box_u, K, the integrand and the measure (Jacobian 1) all inherit it.'
  Verify BOTH properties of u = dT/|dT| symbolically -- they are what the Ward identity rests on.
  [OK  ] partial_c u_mu = 0 identically for all four components -- u is EXACTLY invariant under T -> T + const, with the full nonlinear square root, not to leading order
  [OK  ] u is homogeneous of DEGREE 0 in dT (u(lam dT) - u(dT) = 0 for all components), so any functional of u alone inherits the shift symmetry -- including Box_u, K and the measure

  *** NO PROPERTY OF K IS USED. *** The symmetry lives in the map T -> u, upstream of the
  kernel entirely. So the ALL-ORDERS additive closure -- beta_a0^additive = 0 exactly -- holds
  for alpha=2 verbatim, and would hold for any alpha. This is the strongest of the two-loop
  legs and it is the one that needs no transfer argument at all.
  [OK  ] MUTATION: a frame with an undifferentiated T inserted has partial_c u_0 = 1/sqrt(Derivative(T(t, x, y, z), t)**2 - Derivative(T(t, x, y, z), x)**2 - Derivative(T(t, x, y, z), y)**2 - Derivative(T(t, x, y, z), z)**2) != 0 and BREAKS the shift symmetry -- so the invariance above is a real property of the dT-only construction, not automatic

======================================================================================================
S2. THE EXPLICIT TWO-LOOP TADPOLES -- they vanish on K(0) = 0 ALONE, which alpha=2 satisfies
======================================================================================================
  Lane C: 'EXPLICIT TWO-LOOP TADPOLES (figure-8 + double-bubble): both multiply the frame
  prefactor K(0)*(u.u) = 0 EXACTLY (zero external frame momentum -> resolvent hits K(0);
  confirmed 0 both in the series AND by the full Herglotz measure integral).'
  So the ONLY input is K(0) = 0. Verify it for alpha=2 BOTH ways, as Lane C did for alpha=1:

    (i) closed form:      K_2(0) = 0
  [OK  ] alpha=2 closed form gives K_2(0) = 0 exactly
    (ii) FULL MEASURE:    K_2(0) = 1 - Int_0^1 rho_2/s ds = 1 - 1 = 0
  [OK  ] and the full Herglotz measure integral gives K_2(0) = 0 EXACTLY -- both routes agree, exactly as Lane C required of alpha=1. The figure-8 and double-bubble tadpoles therefore vanish identically on alpha=2 as well
  [OK  ] MUTATION: scaling the measure by 0.9 gives K(0) = 1/10 != 0, which would leave a z-independent frame vertex and RE-OPEN the tadpole channel -- so K(0) = 0 is the whole content of this leg and the check is not vacuous

