S5. BOTH FOOTINGS -- and the honest observation that nothing here depends on a0 at all
======================================================================================================
  Lane C section [4] asks whether anything flips between the two footings. For the transfer
  argument the answer is stronger than 'no': a0 does not appear in ANY of the six legs.

    leg                                  depends on a0?
    (A) shift symmetry                   no -- symmetry
    tadpoles ~ K(0)                        no -- K(0)=0
    (b1) sum rule                        no -- identity
    (b2) no Box_u wavefn renorm          no -- operator
    (b3) counterterms poly in W             no -- mu<=1
    graviton all-n rationing           no -- combinatorial
    [canonical cH_L/Z] a0 = 9.3600e-11 m/s^2 -- enters only as the SCALE inside K(Box_u/a0^2)
    [alternate rho_tot/cH0] a0 = 1.1300e-10 m/s^2 -- enters only as the SCALE inside K(Box_u/a0^2)
  [OK  ] the two footings differ by 21%, and NONE of the six legs references a0's value -- a0 enters only as the scale inside K's argument, which is precisely why the protection statement is about K's ENDPOINTS and symmetries rather than about a0's magnitude

